## Historical-context warning

<Danger>
  **HISTORICAL — ZERO IMPLEMENTATION AUTHORITY.** Do not treat this record as current architecture, instructions, production proof, certification, legal or rights authority, price, availability, or permission to reactivate a concept.
</Danger>

Use these exact boundary values unless a governing source requires a stricter classification:

```yaml
context_mode: historical_only
implementation_authority: none
production_proof: false
current_source_required: true
reactivation_requires_new_review: true
```

## Source identity and classification

| Field | Historical value |
| --- | --- |
| Source title | Replace with exact title |
| Stable source/reference ID | Replace with governed ID; do not invent |
| Source type | Replace: archive, proposal, prior standard, diagram, plan, release note, or other |
| Author/owner at time | Replace or `unresolved` |
| Created/published | Replace with exact date or period |
| Effective period | Replace, `never_effective`, or `unresolved` |
| Historical version | Replace |
| Superseded/archived on | Replace or `unresolved` |
| Historical evidence class | Replace |
| Rights/provenance restriction | Replace |
| Current successor | Root-relative route or `none_identified` |

Source existence proves that the source exists. It does not prove adoption, implementation, production, present authority, correctness, rights clearance, or continuing validity.

## Historical summary

Explain in past tense:

- the problem the source attempted to address;
- the architecture, doctrine, policy, workflow, product, or promise it proposed;
- the scope and assumptions at that time;
- whether it was proposed, accepted, piloted, implemented, or unresolved;
- the evidence that supports that classification.

Do not silently rewrite the historical meaning to match the present system.

## Historical architecture or timeline

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Historical source"] --> B["Historical proposal"]
    B --> C{"Adoption evidence?"}
    C -->|Found| D["Bounded historical state"]
    C -->|Not found| E["Unresolved; no authority"]
    D --> F["Current successor"]
    E --> F
```

Label every diagram node as historical, current, target, unresolved, or superseded. A historical flow is explanatory and must not read like an executable operator procedure.

